  dict(t="box",p=["The next morning, his older sister Maryam — sixteen and carrying her own heavy — sat on his bed. 'Want to know what I learned about sabr? It is not sitting still. Look at Ayyub: years of sickness, lost wealth, lost children — and he never stopped ASKING. He complained TO Allah, not about Allah. Sabr with a voice.' Then she said the words that rearranged Adam's year: 'Baba says: we do our part, we pray, and we trust the Waiting. That is all any of us can carry.'"]),
  dict(t="box",p=["They built the kit without naming it: Adam kept one honest sentence a day to Mama about his anger. Maryam took him to pray — and taught him the two-rak'ah reset when a wave hits. Baba made three job calls every morning like clockwork — sabr with shoes on. And Mama said the verse every night before sleep: <em>fa-inna ma'al 'usri yusra</em> — with hardship comes ease, and it came twice in the Quran so nobody could miss it."]),
  dict(t="wise",p=["'I can hold it. I can pray it. I can work it. I can wait on Allah. I am not a statue and I am not alone.'"]),
