  dict(t="box",p=["Her mother — the wiser half of the house that week — found her on the balcony and said: 'Say it with both hands, habibti. What is hurting?' 'Everything about us changed.' 'Now the other hand. What is real and good?' 'The prize. My writing. Your cooking. Huda's hugs.' Mama sat down beside her: 'Then tonight: alhamdulillah — AND — my heart hurts. Allah is big enough for both. He never asked one to lie about the other.'"]),
  dict(t="box",p=["That night Aisha prayed two rak'ahs of shukr AND made du'a with her forehead down that Allah repair what broke and keep the writing alive in her. She put the certificate on the wall — next to the photo of the old family. Both are true. Both belong there. She was thirteen and already better at the hardest equation in worship than most adults: how to be grateful without lying, and sad without quitting."]),
  dict(t="wise",p=["'Alhamdulillah ala kulli haal — praise in EVERY condition — which includes the one where the tears fall while the tongue thanks.'"]),
  dict(t="cp",c=dict(q="What made the week survivable?",o=[["Naming both — the hurt and the gift — in the same breath, before Allah.",True,"That's honest shukr: it never makes gratitude a mask. Quran 14:7 promises INCREASE to thanks — and Allah also promises the patient that no pain was wasted."],["Deleting the pain to appear grateful.",False,"Masks keep the pain and add shame to it."],["Deleting the gift to stay sad.",False,"The writing, the applause, Mama's cooking — erased from the record? That is ingratitude in the OTHER direction."]])),
