 scenario=dict(q="Yara's team lost the final AND she was named player of the tournament. Her parents keep saying 'be grateful — you lost!' What should she say?",o=[
  ["\"I am grateful for the award AND upset about the loss — both are true tonight.\"",True,"The honest 'both' sentence — exactly the lesson."],["\"You're right — I'll only be happy.\"",False,"The mask — deleting the loss is not shukr."],["\"You're right — I'll only be sad.\"",False,"And deleting the award isn't gratitude either."]],),
 guide_note="Do not demand gratitude as a MOOD. Model the two-hands talk at family dinner. Watch especially in grief, divorce and chronic-illness homes: children get trained to hide joy out of loyalty — release them explicitly ('Jiddu would want you at the picnic'). And 9–10: weeks of gray is a health signal, not an attitude problem.",
